---
title: Pupusas Revueltas
cooklang: 2
servings: 6
cuisine: Salvadoran
source: recipe-pack lunch-2/2435-revueltas-pupusas-1
---

= Chicken chicharrón -> chicharrón

`Heat medium` @oil{1%tbsp} in a #skillet{} over medium heat, `add` @chicken thighs{700%g}(boneless, skin on,
cut into chunks) skin-side down and `cook` until ~{golden and rendered}, ~{15-20%minutes}, stirring
only two or three times.

`Add` @roma tomatoes{2}(chopped), @red bell pepper{1/2}(chopped), @green bell pepper{1/2}(chopped),
@red onion{1/4}(chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @oregano{1%tsp},
@salt{} and @pepper{} and `cook` ~{10-12%minutes} until ~{soft and jammy}. -> chicken mix

`Transfer` the @&chicken mix{} to a #food processor{}, `pulse` until ~{a thick}, smooth paste forms
and `cool`.

= Dough -> dough

`Combine` @masa harina{500%g} with @warm water{700%ml} gradually in a #large bowl{} and `knead`
until ~{the dough is soft}, pliable and moist but not sticky.

= Filling -> filling

`Mix` the @&chicharrón{} with @refried beans{250%g}, @mozzarella{200%g}(shredded) and
@Monterey Jack{200%g}(shredded) in a #+bowl{} until ~{well combined}.

= Assembly and cooking -> pupusas

`Shape` the @&dough{} into @{12} discs on a #board{}. -> discs

`Fill` the @&discs{} on the #&board{} with the @&filling{}, `fold` the edges to encase and `flatten` each into a
12 cm disc. -> pupusas

`Heat medium` a #comal{} over medium heat and `cook` the @&pupusas{} on the #&comal{} for
~{3-5%minutes} per side until ~{golden with charred spots}.

`Serve` warm with @?curtido{} and @?salsa{}.
